<job id="?scan-folder?">

  <ti label="About: Scan a directory">
    <ti>Change the directory or the strategy and see the report again.</ti>
  </ti>

  <ti label="Parameter description">
    <ti label="Directory to scan:">Defines the directory you want to view and scan</ti>
    <ti label="Directory-Levels:">()Directory Levels to Scan,
Defines how many sub-direcotries should be included in the report.
    By default this value is 1. If it is 2(e:s) then one additional directory-hierarchy is included.()</ti>
  <ti label="Strategy:">()This parameter is very essential and defines which strategy in executed.()</ti>
<ti label="()   1) Strategy: life()" flxag="label_right">This is the standard. Whenever you want to view the report of a specific directory(e:s) the directory is scanned on the fly. 
This is good as long as you view just one or two directory-levels. But when you want to scan more directory levels(e:s) this algorithm gets slow. 
Then its time to use the policy 'image'.</ti>
<ti label="()   2) Strategy: image()" fxlag="label_right">This algorithm is usefull if you want to see a lot of directory-levels. The algorithm scans one time the selected directory and all its sub-directories. 
All calculations of directory-sizes and the aggregations are done once. 
This may need some time(e:s) but once it is done(e:s) the reports for one currently viewed directory happens relativly fast.
  </ti>
  <ti label="Limit Files by Kb-Size:">This parameters recudes the files. This may be usefull in order to reduce the amount the the duration.</ti>

  </ti>  
</job>

<job id="?SetupCategories?" role="hidden">

  <ti label="About: Setup: Categories">
